  ▌ sshpick pick [query ...]

  Pick a host from ~/.ssh/config and ssh to it. Exactly one match connects at
  once, without opening the picker.

  Keys:

  Enter                     ssh to the selected host
  Esc, Ctrl-C               quit (exit 130)
  Up, Down, Ctrl-P, Ctrl-N  move
  Ctrl-U                    clear the query
  Ctrl-W                    delete the last word


  Global Options:

  -h,  --help             Output usage information
       --no-color         No color mode (default off)
       --non-interactive  Never open the picker; connect only when exactly one
                          host matches
  -V,  --version          Output the version number


  Examples:

  - Open the picker with every host

    $ sshpick

  - Open it filtered to hosts matching both words

    $ sshpick new consul

  - Connect without the picker when one host matches

    $ sshpick stg-bastion

  - Search for a word that is also a command name

    $ sshpick pick list

  - Search for text that starts with a dash

    $ sshpick -- -bastion
